    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. quick question on the insurance part though—if the cargo gets damaged mid-transit, like during a heavy storm at sea, where does the risk actually transfer from the seller to us (the buyer)? does the seller's responsibility end once the goods are on the ship?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Under CIF, the seller's insurance liability generally terminates once the goods are loaded onto the ship. In other words, the seller's insurance coverage ends once they are relieved of the risk of loss or damage to the goods, typically at the \"assertEquals\" clause (i.e., when the goods are onboard the ship bound for Germany). The risk of damage or loss from that point on belongs to the buyer.",
      "source": "target",
