      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Under CIF, the seller typically needs to provide proof of the incident, such as a detailed report of the damage or loss. They may also need to provide documentary evidence, like photographs, witness statements, or marine surveyor reports, to verify the incident occurred while the goods were under their insurance coverage and before they were loaded onto the ship. The buyer's insurance underwriter will then evaluate the claim.",
